Solar time calculations for calculating "sundial time" in Tcl 9.0

This library calculates the "solar time" for a given location and UTC time.
When interpreted as a UTC time it will have the same day as the "natural"
timezone for your location, and the time will be exactly 12 hours from
midnight to noon, and noon to midnight.  The time will update as you move
around, and the ratio of "solar seconds" to UTC seconds will change only
at noon and midnight.

There may well be some errors in this code, but the daily noon time seems to
be within about a minute of several reliable sources.  Corrections to the
orbital parameter tables are welcome.

-----

Rather than argue for or against switching to DST always, or eliminating
DST altogether, I propose we stop using timezones entirely.

Instead, go back to the "local time zone" - 12 noon is always based on
local noon (the instant when the sun is highest in the sky, which is
what a sun dial always shows).

It worked fine up until they invented time zones so that railroad
timetables could be useful and the telegraph allowed communicating with
someone where the sun was in a different relative position.  Then we
became slaves to the clock, and everyone had to go to school at 7:30
and leave at 3:30 and businesses were open 9 to 5 and who cares if the
clocks were all changed you have to follow the schedule!

So yeah, get rid of DST, don't make it be always, and if 8am is before
sunrise, maybe don't have school start before 8am!

Without the supercomputers everyone walks around with, this would be
difficult, but now that almost everyone has a phone, which has GPS,
you can calculate local noon trivially.  No more one hour jumps each
time you cross a time zone line, the time zone changes as you move.
Your friend 5 miles away on the other side of the line is only 20 seconds
difference from you, not 1 hour.

No spring forward or fall back.  Every place in the contiguous 48 states
would have sunrise before 8am and sunset after 4pm even on the shortest
day, and the southern states would always have sunrise by 7am and sunset
after 5pm.

Use the aptly named UTC for coordinating time over wider areas.  Use Plus
Codes for figuring out the time somewhere else.

And stop being slaves to the Almighty Clock!
